{"format":1,"manifest":{"name":"format-on-save","publisher":"vyloxi","version":"1.0.0","displayName":"Format on Save","description":"Runs a formatter (Prettier, rustfmt, gofmt, black, shfmt...) on a file each time you save it. Off until you turn it on.","engines":{"ferrum":"^0.1.0"},"categories":["Formatters"],"icon":"icon.png","repository":"https://github.com/voukengdongmofrankysteve/ferrum-market","license":"MIT","main":"extension.js","activationEvents":["onStartup"],"permissions":["terminal"],"contributes":{"commands":[{"command":"formatOnSave.toggle","title":"Turn Format on Save On or Off","category":"Format on Save"},{"command":"formatOnSave.now","title":"Format This File Now","category":"Format on Save"},{"command":"formatOnSave.showCommands","title":"Show the Formatter for Each File Type","category":"Format on Save"}],"configuration":{"title":"Format on Save","properties":{"formatOnSave.enabled":{"type":"boolean","default":false,"description":"Run the formatter every time you save."},"formatOnSave.commands":{"type":"string","default":"","description":"A JSON object from file extension to command, with {file} where the path goes. Example: {\"js\": \"npx prettier --write {file}\", \"py\": \"ruff format {file}\"}. Empty uses the built in list."}}}}},"files":{"icon.png":{"encoding":"base64","content":""},"extension.js":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"// Format on Save: runs a formatter command for the file you just saved (Prettier, rustfmt, gofmt, black, shfmt...).\n// The command is typed in the terminal, where you can see it. It is off until you turn it on in the settings.\n// Note: it types into the terminal that is open, so do not use it while a program that reads keys (a server's prompt, a REPL) is running there.\n\nconst DEFAULTS = {\n  js: 'npx prettier --write {file}', jsx: 'npx prettier --write {file}', mjs: 'npx prettier --write {file}', ts: 'npx prettier --write {file}', tsx: 'npx prettier --write {file}',\n  json: 'npx prettier --write {file}', css: 'npx prettier --write {file}', scss: 'npx prettier --write {file}', html: 'npx prettier --write {file}', md: 'npx prettier --write {file}',\n  yml: 'npx prettier --write {file}', yaml: 'npx prettier --write {file}', vue: 'npx prettier --write {file}', svelte: 'npx prettier --write {file}',\n  rs: 'rustfmt {file}', go: 'gofmt -w {file}', py: 'black {file}', sh: 'shfmt -w {file}', tf: 'terraform fmt {file}', dart: 'dart format {file}', kt: 'ktlint -F {file}', php: 'php-cs-fixer fix {file}',\n};\n\n/** Parses the commands setting: a JSON object from extension to command. Anything invalid falls back to the defaults. */\nfunction parseCommands(text) {\n  const t = String(text || '').trim();\n  if (!t) return { ...DEFAULTS };\n  try {\n    const o = JSON.parse(t);\n    if (!o || typeof o !== 'object' || Array.isArray(o)) return { ...DEFAULTS };\n    const out = {};\n    for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(o)) if (typeof v === 'string' && v.includes('{file}') && v.length < 300) out[k.replace(/^\\./, '').toLowerCase()] = v;\n    return Object.keys(out).length ? out : { ...DEFAULTS };\n  } catch {\n    return { ...DEFAULTS };\n  }\n}\n\nconst unsafePath = (p) => /[\"\\n\\r$`]/.test(p);\n\n/** The command for a file, or null when the extension has none or the path is not safe to type. */\nfunction commandFor(path, commands) {\n  if (!path || unsafePath(path)) return null;\n  const ext = path.split('.').pop().toLowerCase();\n  const cmd = commands[ext];\n  return cmd ? cmd.replace(/\\{file\\}/g, '\"' + path + '\"') : null;\n}\n\nexports._test = { parseCommands, commandFor, DEFAULTS };\n\nexports.activate = function (context) {\n  let enabled = ferrum.settings.get('formatOnSave.enabled') === true;\n  let lastRun = { path: '', at: 0 };\n  const commands = () => parseCommands(ferrum.settings.get('formatOnSave.commands'));\n\n  function status() {\n    ferrum.window.setStatusBar('formatOnSave.status', enabled ? { text: 'Format on save', tooltip: 'Format on Save is on. Click to turn it off.', command: 'formatOnSave.toggle' } : { text: '' });\n  }\n  status();\n\n  async function format(path) {\n    const cmd = commandFor(path, commands());\n    if (!cmd) return false;\n    lastRun = { path, at: Date.now() };\n    await ferrum.terminal.run(cmd);\n    return true;\n  }\n\n  context.subscriptions.push(\n    ferrum.events.on('save', async (e) => {\n      if (!enabled || !e || !e.path) return;\n      // Formatting rewrites the file; do not format the same file twice within 4 seconds.\n      if (lastRun.path === e.path && Date.now() - lastRun.at < 4000) return;\n      await format(e.path);\n    }),\n    ferrum.settings.onDidChange((key, value) => {\n      if (key === 'formatOnSave.enabled') { enabled = value === true; status(); }\n    }),\n    ferrum.commands.register('formatOnSave.toggle', () => {\n      enabled = !enabled;\n      status();\n      ferrum.window.showMessage('Format on save is ' + (enabled ? 'on' : 'off') + ' until you restart. Set formatOnSave.enabled in the settings to keep it.');\n    }),\n    ferrum.commands.register('formatOnSave.now', async () => {\n      const doc = await ferrum.editor.active();\n      if (!doc || !doc.path) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Save the file first, then run this again.', 'warn');\n      if (doc.dirty) await ferrum.commands.execute('file.save');\n      if (!(await format(doc.path))) ferrum.window.showMessage('No formatter command is set for .' + doc.path.split('.').pop() + ' files. Add one in the formatOnSave.commands setting.', 'warn');\n    }),\n    ferrum.commands.register('formatOnSave.showCommands', async () => {\n      const c = commands();\n      await ferrum.window.showQuickPick(Object.entries(c).map(([k, v]) => ({ label: '.' + k, detail: v })), { placeholder: 'The formatter for each kind of file' });\n    }),\n  );\n};\n\nexports.deactivate = function () {};\n"},"README.md":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"# Format on Save\n\nWhen you save a file, this types the formatter command for that file type in the terminal, for example `npx prettier --write \"src/app.ts\"`. It is **off by default**. Turn it on with `formatOnSave.enabled` (or the command, for this session only). **Format This File Now** does it once.\n\n## Built in formatters\n\nPrettier for JavaScript, TypeScript, JSON, CSS, SCSS, HTML, Markdown, YAML, Vue and Svelte; `rustfmt`; `gofmt -w`; `black`; `shfmt -w`; `terraform fmt`; `dart format`; `ktlint -F`; `php-cs-fixer fix`. They must be installed. Change or add any with the `formatOnSave.commands` setting (a JSON object, with `{file}` where the path goes).\n\n## Things to know\n\n- The command is **typed into the terminal that is open**. Do not use this while a program that reads keys is running there (a server's prompt, a REPL, a pager): the command would be typed into it.\n- Formatting rewrites the file on disk. The same file is not formatted twice within 4 seconds.\n- Paths with quotes, `$` or backticks are skipped.\n\n## Permissions\n\n**terminal**. It does not read any file.\n"}}}